/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 290 0 R
/T (The rapid emergence of quick commerce in India represents a significant structural evolution of traditional e-commerce, driven by changing consumer expectations and advancements in digital infrastructure. Conventional e-commerce models were historically built around scheduled delivery systems, with fulfillment timelines ranging from same-day to multiple days. However, increasing urbanisation, rising time sensitivity among consumers, and the growing preference for convenience have led to the adoption of ultra-fast delivery models, typically within 10-20 minutes. These platforms operate on a fundamentally different model compared to traditional e-commerce, focusing on speed, proximity, and high-frequency consumption.)
/E (The rapid emergence of quick commerce in India represents a significant structural evolution of traditional e-commerce, driven by changing consumer expectations and advancements in digital infrastructure. Conventional e-commerce models were historically built around scheduled delivery systems, with fulfillment timelines ranging from same-day to multiple days. However, increasing urbanisation, rising time sensitivity among consumers, and the growing preference for convenience have led to the adoption of ultra-fast delivery models, typically within 10-20 minutes. These platforms operate on a fundamentally different model compared to traditional e-commerce, focusing on speed, proximity, and high-frequency consumption.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
