/P 312 0 R
/T (Law is conservative by nature, so AI adoption is cautious. That said, AI is useful for clerical, research, and technical tasks, I've personally used it to ease advisory opinions and research. It saves time in a system known for being slow. The Supreme Court is reportedly building AI tools for case filing and judge allotment. However, blind reliance is dangerous, some advocates were penalized for citing AI-generated, non-existent cases. AI should be a supportive tool, used with caution.)
/E (Law is conservative by nature, so AI adoption is cautious. That said, AI is useful for clerical, research, and technical tasks, I've personally used it to ease advisory opinions and research. It saves time in a system known for being slow. The Supreme Court is reportedly building AI tools for case filing and judge allotment. However, blind reliance is dangerous, some advocates were penalized for citing AI-generated, non-existent cases. AI should be a supportive tool, used with caution.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
